<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX4-QA-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX4-QA-001" ;
  triage:title "Synchronous task-ledger read called inline in the async Tokio list_messages handler, bypassing the control_path_sync_bridge used by every other sync call in storage_and_nudge_router.rs" ;
  triage:description "AX.4 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax4-qa-r1, PR #1194 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T09:14Z; found by arch-qa, reproduced by quality-mgr, corroborated by rust-best-practices-agent) at head aaf2e04bf. crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs async fn list_messages() (line 595) calls atm_core::list::list_task_ledger_with_runtime(query, self.service_runtime) directly. That function (crates/atm-core/src/list.rs:267-300) is fully synchronous and reads through TaskStore/rusqlite, a single-writer-lock backend, so the call can pin a Tokio worker for the query duration including any writer-lock wait. Every other synchronous core operation in this file (clear_messages, heartbeat, queue_get_next, graft_receiver_star) is wrapped in self.control_path_sync_bridge.run(deadline, closure). This is new code in the Tokio+Axum target-architecture crate, not legacy daemon code. Fix: wrap the call in self.control_path_sync_bridge.run(...) exactly as clear_messages does." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ARCH" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T11:20:03Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Blocking finding closed by a later valid Completion and quality-mgr follow-up QA; final sprint verdict AX4-QA4 PASS 0/0/0 (PR #1194 comment 5551411069)." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T09:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AX4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T09:14:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AX4-QA-001/AX4-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

